    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0350" n="338" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Colonel J. G.
                            Shinkle</hi><anchor n="57" xml:id="d121-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to Lieutenant General Alvan C.
                            Gillem, Jr.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-25">25 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>There have been submitted to your office in the past two months certain
                        papers which it was anticipated would be acted upon by the Military
                        Sub-committee. These papers are as follows:<anchor n="58" xml:id="d121-f2"/>
                        <list>
                            <label><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                            <item>“Regulations for Demobilization” together with “Annex A” to that
                                regulation.</item>
                            <label><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                            <item>“Regulations for Reorganization, Redeployment and
                                Integration”.</item>
                            <label><hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</label>
                            <item>“Interim Plan for Formation of Service Areas”.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It is contemplated that members of the two Chinese Parties will be
                        appointed in the near future to the Reorganization Section of Executive
                        Headquarters that they and together with those Americans already appointed,
                        will proceed to Peiping. It is suggested that those <pb facs="0351" n="339"
                            xml:id="pg339"/> papers listed above be considered for approval by
                        Executive Headquarters with the object that an attempt be made to have each
                        paper approved by that agency rather than by the Military
                        Sub-committee.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>It is requested that the suggestion above be approved, that all but one
                        copy of each paper listed above be returned to this office and that no
                        further consideration of the papers be made by the Military Subcommittee
                        unless further requested by Executive Headquarters.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed>J. G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shinkle</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colonel, G. S. G.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
